<title>UK: BOE gives UK money market 55 mln stg further help.</title>
<headline>BOE gives UK money market 55 mln stg further help.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of England said it provided the UK money market with a further 55 million stg of assistance at established interest rates.</p>
<p>Five million stg was allotted outright in bills while 50 million came in repos to August 4.</p>
<p>The Bank has provided liquidity totalling 170 million stg so far on Friday, in response to a forecast money market shortage of 1.65 billion stg.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7708</p>
